section='''\n\n## 34. Turn 34 — one callable chart controller (owner authorized 2026-10-03)\n\n### Current disposition — REBUILDING FROM ACCEPTED TURN 28\nThe prior Turn 33/34 approach is rejected. RCA: Analyze impersonated NOW by mutating global NOW state (`S.index`, `S.level`, `S.nowVisible`, `S.nowComparisons`, active/focus state) and adding Analyze-specific branches to NOW helpers. That is not a reusable chart implementation and allowed Fixed/Horizon to diverge while superficial control-state tests stayed green.\n\n### Construction rule\n- Rebuild directly from accepted `market-navigator-turn28-ship.html`; Turn 30/31/32/33/earlier Turn 34 application artifacts are failure evidence only, never implementation donors.\n- Extract one callable chart controller in the resulting single-file application. NOW and Analyze must call the same controller with explicit arguments; neither may impersonate the other by rewriting its private state.\n- Required public call shape: `MNChart34.open({target, root, series, horizon, display, active})`.\n- NOW call: `MNChart34.open({target:'now', root:S.index, series:visibleIds25(), horizon:S.h, display:S.indexDisplay||'fixed', active:S.nowActive})`.\n- Analyze call: `MNChart34.open({target:'analysis', root:S.analysisRoot, series:[...S.analysisSeries], horizon:S.analysisH26||S.h, display:S.analysisDisplay34||'fixed', active:S.analysisActive})`.\n- The controller alone owns series preparation, Fixed/Horizon transformation, axis planning, chart snapshot/paint preparation and draw dispatch for both targets.\n- Context wrappers may own only navigation/presentation state: root, series list, horizon, display selection, active series, modal open/close. They may not duplicate chart mathematics or series preparation.\n\n### Required behavior\n1. Analyze opens full-size with exactly the selected series as root.\n2. Horizon is modal-local and does not mutate frozen NOW horizon.\n3. Fixed/Horizon is modal-local and changes actual governed-index plotted points, not merely a select value. Fixed uses canonical persistent values; Horizon rebases the same canonical series to 100 at the visible start.\n4. `+ Add`, legend focus/removal, source explainer, crosshair/tooltip, More/actions, AI POV, Data, Print and downloads remain functional.\n5. Eligible two-family comparisons expose Y1+Y2 according to the same controller axis plan.\n6. Closing Analyze leaves NOW byte-for-byte-equivalent analytical state: root, horizon, display, visible/comparison series and chart points.\n\n### Release-blocking proof\n- Static proof: exactly one `MNChart34` controller definition; both NOW and Analyze call `MNChart34.open`; no `S.turn33Analysis`, `surfaceMode32`, `chartSurface31`, `sourceSetStandalone26`, or Analyze branch inside `visibleIds25`.\n- Behavioral proof: capture actual plotted point arrays before and after Fixed/Horizon in NOW and in Analyze for a governed index; each Horizon series must start at 100 and differ from Fixed while canonical evidence remains unchanged.\n- Equivalence proof: invoke NOW and Analyze with identical root/series/horizon/display inputs and require equal prepared chart series/points/mode from the controller.\n- Interaction proof: exercise horizon, Add/remove, explainer, crosshair, More and close/restore with zero page/console errors.\n- No control-presence/value-only test can satisfy a behavioral gate.\n'''
